  "readme": [
    "Hand-maintained. Nothing writes to this file — edit it and commit.",
    "",
    "Two lists, one file, because they answer the same question from opposite",
    "sides: `events` is when the market will be reacting to something, and",
    "`marketCalendar` is when there is no market to react. The staleness guard",
    "reads the second so it stops calling a holiday a failed data feed, and the",
    "home page reads the first.",
    "",
    "`confirmed: false` means the date was derived from a pattern rather than",
    "read off an official calendar. The UI marks those, and they should be",
    "replaced as the real dates publish:",
    "  - FOMC decisions  federalreserve.gov/monetarypolicy/fomccalendars.htm",
    "  - CPI and PPI     bls.gov/schedule/news_release",
    "  - Jobs report     bls.gov/schedule/news_release/empsit.htm",
    "  - Market calendar nyse.com/markets/hours-calendars",
    "",
    "CPI and PPI dates below are ESTIMATES on the usual mid-month pattern and",
    "are all unconfirmed. FOMC dates come from the published 2026 calendar.",
    "Jobs-report dates are the first Friday of each month, which is the rule",
    "BLS follows except when it collides with a holiday - the two that do are",
    "marked unconfirmed.",
    "",
    "Times are New York wall clock, 24-hour. Importance is high | medium | low;",
    "only `high` triggers the warning that positioning levels are less reliable."
  ],

